-- title:
--   Degree-two Vélu step equals the order-two Vélu quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field with $2 \neq 0$ and let $E$ be a Weierstrass curve over $L$. Let $H$ be a finite cyclic additive subgroup of the group $E(L)$ of points of the associated affine curve, and let $(x_0,y_0)$ be a nonsingular point of $E$ whose corresponding affine point lies in $H$ and satisfies $\mathrm{veluGy}(x_0,y_0) = -(2y_0 + a_1x_0 + a_3) = 0$. Assume further that the discriminant of Vélu's order-two quotient curve $E' := E.\mathrm{veluQuotient2}\,x_0\,y_0$, the curve with the same $a_1,a_2,a_3$ and with $a_4' = a_4 - 5g_x$, $a_6' = a_6 - b_2 g_x - 7x_0g_x$ where $g_x = 3x_0^2 + 2a_2x_0 + a_4 - a_1y_0$, is nonzero, and let $\varphi : E(L) \to E'(L)$ be an additive homomorphism whose underlying function is `veluPointMap2` (zero to zero, affine points with abscissa $x_0$ to zero, all other points to their Vélu image). The conclusion is an equality of dependent pairs (curve together with a subgroup of its points): the pair consisting of $E.\mathrm{stepCurve}\,H\,2$, namely the curve $\mathrm{twoVeluCurve}$ formed from the set of abscissae of the nonzero points of $H$ killed by $2$, and of $E.\mathrm{stepSubgroup}\,H\,2$, the subgroup of that curve generated by the nonzero points whose abscissa lies in the image, under the step abscissa map $\mathrm{twoVeluX}$ for that same set, of the set of abscissae of the points $P \in H$ with $2P \neq 0$, equals the pair $(E', \varphi(H))$.
--
--   This identifies the degree-two stage of the abscissa-indexed iterated Vélu construction with the classical order-two Vélu quotient by the unique two-torsion point of the cyclic subgroup $H$, together with the image of $H$ under the corresponding two-isogeny. It is used in the computation of $j(E/H)$ and in the resulting descriptions of roots of modular polynomials and of Tate-curve base changes on modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_stepCurve_stepSubgroup_two_eq.lean

